t;&lt;b&gt;387&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr style=&quot;background-color:#E3EEF9;&quot;&gt;&lt;td colspan=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;2 BHK&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;MASTER BEDROOM&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;8′-2″ × 12′-3″ + 4′-4″ × 4′-10″&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;122&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;BATH 1&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;4′-0″ × 7′-0″&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;28&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;LIVING&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;12′-7″ × 12′-2″&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;153&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;BEDROOM 2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;9′-6″ × 10′-0″&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;95&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;KITCHEN&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;6′-2″ × 10′-0″&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;61&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;DINING&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;11′-8″ × 10′-0″ + 4′-4″ × 2′-4″&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;127&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;BATH 2&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;4′-0″ × 7′-3″&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;29&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;BALCONY&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;16′-0″ × 3′-10″&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;61&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;2 BHK total (excl. balcony)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;614&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=visible;rounded=0;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1F2D3D;" vertex="1" parent="D-sep-notes"><mxGeometry x="230.00" y="1110.00" width="640.00" height="560.00" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;What this option changes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;1 BHK moved to the west (A–B bay), 2 BHK to the east (B–D bays) next to the stair.&lt;/b&gt; 1 BHK 387 sq ft (plan A 311) · 2 BHK 614 sq ft (plan A 698).&lt;br&gt;• Party wall on the &lt;b&gt;B line&lt;/b&gt; (10″, B1–B3 inside it). The C line becomes an internal wall; a wide opening between C2 and C3 joins the living and the dining.&lt;br&gt;• &lt;b&gt;No passage&lt;/b&gt; (0 sq ft): every door opens straight into a living area.&lt;br&gt;• 1 BHK: bedroom with attached bath, 6′ galley kitchen on the highway wall, living at the entrance. No balcony – the back strip belongs to the 2 BHK.&lt;br&gt;• 2 BHK: master + attached bath (north), living (south, beside the party wall), dining / kitchen / Bedroom 2 / common bath / balcony in the east bay.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Reading this plan&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;① &lt;b&gt;Connecting door&lt;/b&gt; – 3′-0″ in the B-line party wall between the two living rooms. &lt;b&gt;Locked&lt;/b&gt; here; open it = page 2.&lt;br&gt;② 1 BHK entrance (west, 30 ft from the stair) · ③ 2 BHK entrance (east) – both off the shared 4′ gallery.&lt;br&gt;④ Existing stair – assumed at the east (D3) end of the gallery.&lt;br&gt;⑤ Balcony – back strip above C1–D1, for Bedroom 2 and the kitchen.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Trade-off&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• The 1 BHK gets bigger and the 2 BHK tighter: the master is 8′-2″ wide. Splitting on the C line (option C) keeps the 2 BHK comfortable.&lt;br&gt;• Left 4′ strip = baths, kitchen and windows only. Every pillar sits inside a wall.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Engineer to confirm&lt;/b&gt; – the C2–C3 opening needs a beam above; cantilever points as plan A." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=visible;rounded=0;fontSize=12;fontColor=#1F2D3D;" vertex="1" parent="D-sep-notes"><mxGeometry x="920.00" y="1110.00" width="800.00" height="560.00" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram><diagram id="D-3bhk" name="D · 3 BHK (merged)"><mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="1000" grid="1" gridSize="12" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1900" pageHeigh